Reversible Vitrification via Tardigrade CAHS Proteins (Tardigrada)
Microscopic tardigrades survive near-total desiccation (anhydrobiosis) by expressing Cytoplasmic Abundant Heat Soluble (CAHS) proteins. CAHS proteins are intrinsically disordered structures that remain soluble under extreme thermal stress. Upon water loss, CAHS proteins undergo concentration-dependent self-assembly into helical filaments, forming a protective, glass-like amorphous matrix (vitrification).
